  "markdown_content": "The United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO) has added the manuscripts of two foundational Indian texts to its prestigious Memory of World Register. The inscribed works include the *Bhagavad Gita*, one of Hinduism's most sacred philosophical texts, and the *Natyashastra*, an ancient treatise on the performing arts.\\n\\nThis recognition acknowledges these manuscripts' extraordinary cultural and historical importance in world heritage. The Memory of World Register serves as a global repository documenting humanity's documentary heritage.",
